--TEST--
`[int $a, string $b] = $value;` is the subscripts it is spelled out of — positional, keyed, skipped, nested, and throwing on an absent key — `rule:types/declaration` and `rule:types/grammar`.3 and 5, `rule:expressions/bracket-destructuring`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Every leaf is an element read: a positional one names `rule:types/arrays`'s
// normalized key for its own position in the pattern, so `$words[0]` and
// `$words[1]` here — the two entries written with no key of their own.
array<string> $words = ["a" => "alpha", "b" => "beta", "one", "two"];
[string $zero, string $one] = $words;
echo $zero, "|", $one, "\n";
// An explicit `key =>` element reads that key instead, in the pattern's
// own order and independent of where the entry sits.
["b" => string $second, "a" => string $first] = $words;
echo $first, "|", $second, "\n";
// A skipped slot still occupies its position, so `$secondOfTwo` is
// position 1 — the entry keyed `1`, not the second entry in the array.
[, string $secondOfTwo] = $words;
echo $secondOfTwo, "\n";
// `rule:types/conversion`'s one implicit conversion reaches a leaf like any other
// declared position: the element is an `int` and the binding is a `float`.
array<int> $nums = [1, 2, 3];
[float $widened] = $nums;
echo $widened, "\n";
// A nested target takes the element apart in turn, reading through it
// rather than copying it.
array<array<string>> $rows = [["r0c0", "r0c1"], ["r1c0"]];
[[string $c0, string $c1]] = $rows;
echo $c0, "|", $c1, "\n";

class Pair {
    public static function make(): array<string> {
        return ["fresh", "temporary"];
    }
}

// The subject is evaluated once, whatever the pattern's shape, and a
// value nothing else owns is released when the statement ends.
[string $t0, string $t1] = Pair::make();
echo $t0, "|", $t1, "\n";

// A leaf whose key names no entry throws, exactly as the subscript it is
// spelled out of would — `rule:types/absent-storage-is-never-a-zero-value`'s divergence from PHP, which
// warns and binds `null`. The leaves before it have already bound.
try {
    [string $p, string $q, string $r] = $words;
    echo $p, $q, $r, "\n";
} catch (Throwable $e) {
    echo "caught: ", $e->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
one|two
alpha|beta
two
1
r0c0|r0c1
fresh|temporary
caught: undefined array key `2`
